You let Gawaine die an ignoble death in the Forest Perilous.	你讓高文死於派瑞樂斯森林，落得一個不光彩的下場。
You sacrificed Launcelot to the curse of your jealousy.	你因一己妒念的詛咒，犧牲了蘭斯洛特。
You did nothing to save the noble Galahad within the catacombs.	你未曾伸出援手，任由高尚的葛拉漢死在地下墓窖之中。
And so you, your kingdom, and all your poor people perish for lack of a king with moral strength. We end not in glory, but with the bitter taste of ashes and dust and black defeat.	於是你、你的王國，以及所有可憐的子民，都因缺了一位有德行的君王而滅亡。我們的旅程並非終於榮耀，而是終於灰燼、塵土與黑暗敗亡的苦澀滋味。
Your mule has had the sense to run away from the cobras.	你的騾子倒有幾分見識，懂得躲開眼鏡蛇逃走。
If that is truly your wish, that is what you shall have of me.	若這確實是你的心願，我便如你所願。
Alas! You are helpless, completely under Fatima's fatal spell. And here is the reward for your weakness, being strangled to death by Fatima.	唉！你已無力反抗，全然受制於法提瑪的致命咒法。而你軟弱的下場，便是被法提瑪活活勒死。
How will I ever explain this to the queen? Tsk- tsk.	我該如何向王后解釋這一切？嘖，嘖。
By giving this purse, you show further proof that you are free of the need to gain material wealth. You grow more and more worthy in my eyes.	交出這個錢囊，更加證明你已超脫對財富的貪求。在我眼中，你愈發顯得堪當此任。
The Test awaits behind this door. Six tablets, each engraved with a symbol of a Goddess, rest next to a stone plaque with six niches.	考驗就在這扇門後等著你。六塊石板，各刻著一位女神的標識，靜置於一塊有六個凹龕的石匾旁。
Six questions I will pose. You must know to which Goddess the question belongs and place her symbol into the proper niche.	我將提出六個問題。你必須辨明每個問題屬於哪位女神，並將她的標識放入正確的凹龕。
When all six symbols have been placed, I will tell you whether you have passed or failed. If you fail, you may try again.	待六個標識全數安放，我便會告訴你成敗。若是失敗，你可以再試一次。
But there is one more thing I require of you, a gesture to show that you are not bound by material possessions. Give me your purse.	但我還要求你做一件事——以此表明你不受身外之物所束縛。把你的錢囊交給我。
The door is opened. The Test awaits you.	門開了。考驗正等著你。
Arthur?  Arthur.	亞瑟？亞瑟。
Arthur, WAKE UP!	亞瑟，醒醒！
You slept through the entire docking and unloading of the ship.  You indulged too heavily in foreign wine.	你把整段靠港卸貨的過程都睡過去了。你貪杯，喝了太多異國美酒。
If your head is pounding, blame no one but yourself.	若你頭痛欲裂，也怪不得別人，只能怪你自己。
Sir, I am Hazm.  My master sends his respects and invites you to accept his hospitality.  My Master--	大人，小的是哈慈。我家主人向您致意，邀您接受他的款待。我家主人——
Ignore this boy.  You are lucky he did not make off with your mule.  I am Jabir ibn Hamid.  I overheard some sailors say you need a guide through the desert to Jerusalem.	別理這孩子。算你走運，他沒把你的騾子順手牽走。我是賈比耳·伊本·哈米德。我聽幾個水手說，你需要一位嚮導，帶你穿越沙漠前往耶路撒冷。
Please, sir, my Master is Al-Sirat and he is very wise and he asks--	大人，求求您，我家主人是 Al-Sirat，他非常睿智，他想問——
Al-Sirat is an impoverished old scholar of no use to anyone.  But I, Jabir, know the desert, every rock, wadi, and waterhole.  Trust me in all things.	Al-Sirat 不過是個窮困潦倒、百無一用的老學究。但我，賈比耳，熟知這片沙漠的一草一木——每塊岩石、每條旱谷、每處水潭。凡事都信任我便是。
Sir, I beg you to accept my Master's hospitality.  He heard of you from the Captain of the ship and he sends warning that the mukhtar of Gaza--	大人，求您接受我家主人的款待。他從船長那裡聽聞您的事，特地遣人示警，說加薩的村長——
Allow ME to explain.  The mukhtar is the man who governs this port.  He hates all foreigners and if he catches you here, he will throw you in prison.  We should leave at once.	讓「我」來解釋吧。村長是治理這座港口的人。他痛恨一切外邦人，若被他逮到你在此，會把你關進大牢。我們該立刻離開。
I can take you to my Master by secret ways and Al-Sirat will protect and tell you--	我能帶您走密道去見我家主人，Al-Sirat 會保護您，並告訴您——
Get out of here, boy! We men have business together and have no need of chattering pests.  Be off!	滾開，臭小子！我們大人有正事要談，用不著你這種嘮叨的討厭鬼。走開！
Stranger, you will never survive the desert without my help.  I ask for no payment now.  When we reach Jerusalem safely, I will accept a fair payment.	陌生人，沒有我的幫助，你絕不可能在這片沙漠中活下來。我現在分文不取，待我們平安抵達耶路撒冷，再收一份公道的酬勞。
Hire me and I shall guide you to Jerusalem at once.	雇用我，我立刻帶你前往耶路撒冷。
Sir, I beg you, ask to see my Master and all will be well.	大人，求求您，去見見我家主人吧，一切自會安好。
May I advise caution here? Do not rush to use the elixir until it seems absolutely necessary.	容我在此進一言：切莫急著用掉解藥，除非確有絕對必要。
Aye, do what you will with it. Though it will cure the poison, it will never cleanse you of the crime of noble Galahad's death.	正是，這藥你便隨意處置吧。它雖能解毒，卻永遠洗刷不了高尚的葛拉漢因你而死這樁罪過。
The miraculous elixir burns like fire through your veins as it purges you of the poison. You are entirely cured....as long as you are not bitten again.	這神奇的解藥在你血脈中如火燒灼，將毒素滌盡。你已痊癒……只要別再被咬一次。
The apple's potent spell has relieved your hunger and thirst and given you a new surge of strength.	蘋果那股強效的魔力，解去了你的飢渴，也為你注入一股新生的力量。
But alas, it cannot stop the poison of the rat's bite from killing you, it can only delay the final end.	但可惜，它擋不住老鼠咬傷的毒性致你於死地，只能延緩那最終的結局。
Alas, the rat's poison has taken its toll and the cold hand of Death has closed upon you forever.	唉，老鼠的毒液終究奪去了你的性命，死神冰冷的手，永遠攫住了你。
Your horse has no desire to swim in the harbour.	你的坐騎毫無興致在港灣裡游泳。
Your armour and steel drags you to the bottom and there you will lie until you are rotten, soggy and pulpy and truly forgotten.	你的盔甲與鋼鐵把你拖向海底，你將長眠於此，直至腐朽、泡爛、化為爛泥，徹底被人遺忘。
As fortune would have it, this ship is the very one you need.  Ignore the Greek name.  It was sold by a Greek trader and the new owner has yet to paint in the new name.	幸運的是，這艘船正是你所需要的那艘。別在意那個希臘船名，它是一個希臘商人賣出的，新船主還沒來得及漆上新名字。
May your journey be safe and swift, god willing.  You may board now.	願神保佑你此行平安順遂。你現在可以上船了。
Well, at last you have learned to take my advice.	好，你總算學會聽我的勸告了。
You cannot do that from here.	你在此處無法這麼做。
Nothing remains of the pillar here but the indentation where its base once rested.	這根石柱如今只剩下柱基原本所在的凹痕，別無他物。
This pillar did not move. Pause and think before your next choice.	這根石柱紋風不動。下一步之前，先停下來想清楚。
The pillar did not move. I hope you do not intend to waste more of your valuable energy in such pointless exercise.	石柱依然不動。希望你不打算再把寶貴的力氣，浪費在這種徒勞之舉上。
There is no where to go from here. High walls without windows or doors bar the way.	從這裡無路可去。高牆聳立，既無窗也無門，擋住了去路。
Truly you are a hardy man to have come so far.  But you need water!   Waste no time.  Follow me at once.	你確實是個堅毅之人，才能走到這一步。但你需要水！別再耽擱，立刻跟我來。
You have killed the Saracen in a fair fight, and now his soul transforms into a dove and rises into the sky and vanishes from sight.	你在公平的決鬥中殺死了撒拉遜武士，此刻他的靈魂化作一隻鴿子，直上雲霄，消失在天際。
You would not enjoy that.  These rocks are hot enough to toast nuts.	你不會喜歡這麼做的。這些岩石燙得足以烤熟堅果。
The ground is rocky and as hot as the furnaces of Hades.	地面遍佈岩石，炙熱得如同冥府的熔爐。
Hot as it is, you are better off wearing it than carrying it, and you must not even consider leaving it behind.	儘管炙熱難耐，穿著它總比扛著它好，你更不該考慮把它丟下。
In this heat, such a burden would soon kill her.	在這種酷熱之下，這樣的負擔很快就會要了她的命。
You sold the mule, Arthur.	亞瑟，你已經把騾子賣了。
The mule is not here.	騾子不在此處。
You have no waterskin, sad to say.	說來遺憾，你身上沒有水袋。
First you must find one.	你得先找到一個才行。
There is no snake here.	此處並無蛇蹤。
The last thing you need to carry is a rock hot enough to burn your fingers.	你最不需要的，就是帶著一塊燙得能灼傷手指的石頭。
It would be a staggering waste of energy, even if it were possible, but these cliffs are steep and offer no grip for hand or foot.	就算辦得到，也是白白浪費驚人的力氣，何況這些懸崖陡峭，手腳都無處可攀。
It is a terrible shame that Gaza was closed to you, or you might have obtained a waterskin there.	加薩對你緊閉城門，實在可惜，否則你或許能在那裡弄到一個水袋。
Now???	現在？？？
We are here, habib, at the water.	我們到了，朋友，這裡就是水源。
We are on our way to water now, habib.	我們現在正往水源去，朋友。
You waste precious breath talking to the air.	你對著空氣說話，白白浪費寶貴的力氣。
Rather redundant, Arthur, since he is dead.	亞瑟，這話說了也是多餘，他已經死了。
The heat must be affecting your brain.  There is no sign of Jabir.	這暑熱想必是影響了你的腦子。此處毫無賈比耳的蹤跡。
You would find only barren ground.	你只會找到一片荒蕪的地面。
It broke under the ferocity of your assault and is of no use whatsoever.	它在你猛烈的攻擊下碎裂，如今毫無用處。
You can hardly do that from here.	你在此處幾乎無法這麼做。
The heat has affected your thinking, I perceive.	依我看，這酷熱已經影響了你的思緒。
Aye, an excellent idea, provided you can find some.	正是，這主意再好不過了，前提是你得先找得到。
You must return to Jerusalem at once and finish your dealings with Fatima.	你必須立刻返回耶路撒冷，把與法提瑪之間的事了結。
I can give you little more than encouragement and observation where this desert is concerned.	說到這片沙漠，我能給你的，不過是幾句鼓勵與觀察罷了。
This is a desert of extreme terrain.  Sudden cliffs rise and block your way, while wadis unexpectedly appear in the ground.	這是一片地形險惡的沙漠。峭壁驟然聳起擋住去路，旱谷也會在地面上不經意地冒出來。
She is well.  She prays daily for your safety and ministers to Launcelot as he recovers from the Ice Maiden's spell.	她安好。她日日為你的平安祈禱，並照料著蘭斯洛特，他正從冰霜仙子的咒法中康復。
She prays daily for your well-being and success, and for the safe return of Launcelot.	她日日祈禱你平安順遂、大功告成，也祈禱蘭斯洛特平安歸來。
With the tender help of Gwenhyver and her ladies, he is recovering very well from his frozen sojourn.	有昆海兒與她的侍女悉心照料，他從那段冰封的遭遇中恢復得相當好。
Alas, you have not saved Launcelot.  Thus you have jeopardized the success of your entire mission.	唉，你未能救回蘭斯洛特。如此一來，你已使整趟使命的成敗陷入危殆。
I hope you remember the way back to Jerusalem.  It would not do to get lost now.	希望你還記得回耶路撒冷的路。事到如今，可不能迷路。
There is no sign of Jerusalem yet.	目前還看不見耶路撒冷的蹤影。
You should avoid the huge, flat areas of desert plateau, unless you have reason to think there is water there.	你該避開那片廣袤平坦的沙漠台地，除非你有理由相信那裡有水。
There are some hills in the distance, and the ground rises steadily toward the north and east.	遠處有幾座丘陵，地勢朝北方與東方緩緩升高。
There is no snake here, fortunately, for the cobras of this desert are quite lethal.	幸好此處並無蛇蹤，這片沙漠裡的眼鏡蛇可是相當致命。
The lizards in this area are swift and harmless.	這一帶的蜥蜴行動敏捷，但無害。
That is not important now.  You must get back to Jerusalem.	這事眼下並不要緊。你必須回到耶路撒冷去。
I have no knowledge of where water may be hidden in a wadi or oasis.  You must search.	旱谷或綠洲裡的水究竟藏在何處，我毫無所知。你得自己找。
Well, you know where the Pool of Siloam is.	好吧，你知道西羅亞池在哪裡。
I cannot help you find water.  I have no such intimate knowledge of this desert.	我幫不了你找水，我對這片沙漠沒有那樣深入的了解。
Let us hope you remember the way well enough.	但願你把路記得夠清楚。
There is no hint of where to go in this trackless desert.	在這片無跡可循的沙漠裡，看不出該往哪裡走。
Even the shadows provide little relief from the heat.	就連陰影也難以緩解這股酷熱。
The shifting sands erase any traces of where you have been.	流動的沙丘抹去了你曾經走過的一切痕跡。
You have most prudently slain him.	你極為明智地殺了他。
Jabir waits for you to follow him.	賈比耳等著你跟上他。
There is no apparent sign of him, but that means little with such a cunning desert dweller.	表面上不見他的蹤影，但面對這樣狡猾的沙漠住民，這說明不了什麼。
Your brain invents delusions from lack of water and the intense heat.  Do not dwell upon it.	缺水與酷暑，讓你的腦子憑空生出幻象。別放在心上。
A mirage is usually an illusion of water, a bizarre phenomenon of the deserts.	海市蜃樓通常是水的幻象，是沙漠裡一種奇特的現象。
Copper or tin!  Copper or tin! Copper or tin for Widdershins! I am no troll but that is my toll! Copper or tin for Widdershins! Give me my way or a trick I will play!	銅幣或錫幣！銅幣或錫幣！銅幣或錫幣，敬獻 Widdershins！我不是山怪，這是我的買路錢！銅幣或錫幣，敬獻 Widdershins！依我便罷，不然就讓你嚐嚐我的把戲！
Copper or tin!  Copper or tin! Copper or tin for Widdershins! I am no troll but that is my toll! Copper or tin for Widdershins!	銅幣或錫幣！銅幣或錫幣！銅幣或錫幣，敬獻 Widdershins！我不是山怪，這是我的買路錢！銅幣或錫幣，敬獻 Widdershins！
The trick has been played and I fear the sprite's bolt of mischief was aimed squarely at your purse.	詭計已然使出，恐怕這妖精那道搗蛋的咒力，正好衝著你的錢囊而來。
You were thrown back by a sorcerous barrier of great power. Yet there must be a way to pass it.	你被一道法力強大的魔障彈了回來。但想必總有通過它的辦法。
I suspect these five stones are a part of the riddle you must solve to breach the barrier.	我懷疑，這五塊石頭正是你破解那道魔障必須解開的謎題的一部分。
Eh, what is this? Why are you--ah, what a wonderful smell these herbs have! How very potent and aromatic! I shall hang them up at once.	咦，這是什麼？你怎麼——啊，這些藥草的香氣真是絕妙！好濃郁、好芬芳！我這就把它們掛起來。
What, are you a merchant, too? What do I want with herbs? Ah, but they do smell good. In fact, they are so strongly aromatic, they might help disguise the smell of my fish.	什麼，你也是個商人？我要藥草做什麼？啊，不過它們聞起來確實不錯。說真的，香氣這麼濃郁，說不定還能蓋過我這些魚的氣味。
Very well, I will take them. Here are 2 fals, all I can afford. I am a poor man.	好吧，我收下了。這是兩枚銅幣，我只出得起這些了。我是個窮人。
You have taught me something, habibi. Rather than dwelling only upon my problems, had I but sought a solution, I would have been a happier man.	你教會了我一件事，朋友。與其一味沉溺於自己的難題，倒不如尋求解方，那樣我早該活得更快樂。
I thank you for this piece of wisdom, which will benefit my neighbors as well as myself. Sa'alam aleikem.	感謝你賜下這番智慧之言，這對我的鄰人與我自己都有益處。Sa'alam aleikem。
You cannot go this way.  There is a thief loose in the bazaar and many merchants are complaining.  The Jaffa Gate will be locked while we search for him.	你不能走這條路。市集裡出了個賊，許多商人都在抱怨。賈法城門將封閉，直到我們找到他為止。
We do not know who he is, but when we find him, he is a dead man.  Now move along, before we begin to suspect that YOU may be the thief.	我們還不知道他是誰，但一旦找到，他就是個死人。現在快走開，免得我們開始懷疑「你」就是那個賊。
You may enter, stranger, but you may not leave until we have finished searching the city for thieves.	陌生人，你可以進去，但在我們搜遍全城捉賊之前，你不得離開。
Aye, and if you are a thief, you will wish you had never come here.	正是，你若是賊，必會後悔自己踏進這裡。
No, Arthur, no!	不，亞瑟，不要！
Alas! You are helpless, completely under Fatima's fatal spell. And here is the reward for your weakness, being smothered to death by a perfumed pillow.	唉！你已無力反抗，全然受制於法提瑪的致命咒法。而你軟弱的下場，便是被一只薰香的枕頭活活悶死。
Gladly will I sell you relic. But first you must tell me -- what is the name of the saint whose relic you wish to buy?	我很樂意賣你聖物。但你得先告訴我——你想買的是哪位聖徒的聖物？
Saint %s! Yes, I do have a relic of Saint %s. Normally, 3 dinar, on sale today for 2 dinars. But I like you. You have an honest face. So for you, only 1 dinar!	聖%s！沒錯，我這裡確實有聖%s的聖物。原價三枚金幣，今日特價兩枚金幣。不過我喜歡你，你長了一張老實臉，所以就便宜賣你，只要一枚金幣！
No, no. I must have the name of the saint whose relic you wish to buy. Nothing else will do. Think it over. If you are still interested in buying a relic, just say so.	不，不對。我必須知道你想買的聖物是哪位聖徒的。別的都不算數。你好好想想，若還想買聖物，儘管開口。
Greetings, King Arthur.	亞瑟王，向您致意。
That was quick m'lord.	好快啊，吾王。
Well we meet again, m'lord.  Alas, you have not recovered your mule, I see.	咱們又見面了，吾王。唉，看來你還沒找回你的騾子。
M'lord, your mule has bolted!	吾王，您的騾子脫韁跑了！
How colourful!	好個生動的用詞！
I am sure you never learned such language from me.	我確信這種言語，你絕非跟我學的。
It would seem that being a king does not guarantee gentility.	看來身為國王，未必就保證了溫文儒雅。
May your mouth rot and your tongue wither.	願你嘴巴腐爛，舌頭枯萎。
No wonder Gwenhyver prefers Launcelot, from whose refined lips such words were never spoken.	難怪昆海兒偏愛蘭斯洛特，他那雙優雅的嘴唇，從不曾吐出這種話。
You are speaking gibberish.	你說的是無意義的胡言亂語。
This must be some strange foreign tongue.	這想必是某種陌生的異邦語言。
There are times when even I, Merlin, am without an answer.	即便是我，梅林，也有無言以對的時候。
Your words are clear enough, but your meaning eludes me.	你的話語清楚明白，但你的用意，我卻捉摸不透。
I feel I should know what you want, but your purpose is not clear.	我覺得自己該明白你想要什麼，但你的意圖並不清晰。
You don't see anything particularly interesting.	你沒看見什麼特別有趣的東西。
